{Big Blunder at Bognor by B. H Wood. A Midland contingent stronger than usual
is doing well in the international tournament at Bognor Regis. Here are three
of their games; but first the picture of my monumental blunder in the third
round, which will cheer up a lot of people who imagine they are the only
people who do blunder won games away. Black (to play) can win White's d-pawn
in a variety of ways, e.g. 1...Ba6 followed by 2...Kd6, 3...Ne5 and 4...Bb7;
there is really nothing White can do about it. Instead} 1... Ne5 $4 2. d6+ Kxd6
3. Bxb7 {Source: Birmingham Daily Post - Thursday 17 April 1958} 1-0

