Manchester Guardian, 1 May 1958; Sunday Times, 11 May 1958. Re Dragutin Dimc,
the obit in CHESS, 20 Aug 1958, p335: "Dimc, the Yugoslav student player who
competed at Bognor and whose modest and pleasant demeanour made him popular
with all, has been drowned at Zagreb. He went bathing on a scorchingly hot day.
Heart failure is suspected."} 1-0

