1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3 Be7 6. d4 Bf6 7. dxe5 Nxe5 8.
Nxe5 Bxe5 9. Bxf7+ Kxf7 10. Qd5+ Kf8 11. Qxe5 d6 {"first played in A.Hall-R.A.
Harris, Bognor Regis 1958." (Play The Evans Gambit by Harding & Cafferty 
(Cadogan 1997), p38) No further moves, no result given. But it was actually A.
Hall-G.F.Harris, Bognor Regis 1958, as a game with those colours was played in
the Stevenson Memorial in that year and reported in the Times as follows: "A.
Hall, of Oxford University, had his Evans Gambit opening accepted by G. F.
Harris, of Worcestershire, who adopted an unusual defence leading to one of
the shortest recorded draws in this open�ing - in 15 moves." (The Times, 18
April 1958)} 1/2-1/2

